{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3637937,"ns":0,"title":"Formal fallacy","extract":"In logic and philosophy, a formal fallacy is a pattern of reasoning with a flaw in its logical structure (the logical relationship between the premises and the conclusion). A formal fallacy is contrasted with an informal fallacy.","description":"Faulty deductive reasoning due to a logical flaw","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}